  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Disabling a PhysBone that has \"Reset When Disabled\" turned off retains its last position. \n\nHowever, if I then make my avatar transition (with a nonzero transition time) to a new animation state that changes the bone chain's position, the bone chain instantly snaps back to rest position on the first frame of transition and adds in the next animation step on top of that.\n\nThis is a bit jarring when I want to create smooth transitions between PhysBone-based movement and movement made from animation clips; for instance, maybe I want my bone chain to move to a different resting position while it's not under PhysBones without the moment I disable the PhysBone component being blatantly obvious.",
